### LF teacher
- K004: v3 LF->MK baseline (resnet18, 23 LED + phase): FOV .707 | batch-held-out .494/.471; signal mostly cell type (3-class oracle >= model on gated cells, CD16 .95 vs .88; within-class r .08-.45); CD19/CD56/CD123 collapse across batches. GOAL best .4835 -> superseded by K008/K010 (GOAL re-based on v4; the collapse was label artefact, K007) [verified] (N006; N006-supervised-lf-mk-baseline-on-curated-tar/n006v3_summary.csv, noise_seed_reruns.csv) {cites:3}
- K017: SSL LF encoders are weak as frozen linear probes (FOV .52 vs supervised .71; batch-held-out aug .486/.472 ~ supervised .491/.475, xillum worse .460/.435) but give the best teacher once fine-tuned (K010) [verified] (N007, N014; N007-ssl-pretraining-of-the-lf-encoder-cross/probe_batch_holdout.csv) {cites:2}
- K018: Adversarial domain invariance (DANN) is flat or harmful in every setting tried: GS slide (N010, .284-.308 all within noise), LF batch (N014, .5541 vs .5545), PBC unconditional (N020, unstable) and anchored (N021, harmful) [partial: N010 numbers only in the item text] (N010, N014, N020, N021; N014-teacher-v4-portfolio-resnet50-x15-ep-ssl/n014_goal.csv) {cites:4}
